{
  "summary": "The discussion has over-indexed on extraction boundaries while neglecting the actual highest-leverage first move: consolidating the inline Rich-markup escaping duplication that makes every extraction boundary messier than it needs to be. The code at lines 310-483 (_build_feature_detail_widgets) contains 7 separate instances of the identical pattern `.replace('[', '\\\\[').replace(']', '\\\\]').replace('{', '\\\\{').replace('}', '\\\\}')` followed by `re.sub(r'([%])', r'\\\\\\1', ...)` — but _escape_markup at line 280 already handles all of these characters correctly (it was updated since earlier rounds claimed it missed '{'/'}' — it now handles them at lines 284-286). This means every inline escaping block in _build_feature_detail_widgets is dead duplication that can be replaced with a call to the existing _escape_markup function right now, with zero behavioral risk. This is a ~35-line reduction and, more importantly, it eliminates the tangled escaping logic that blurs the extraction boundary between 'pure helpers' and 'widget builders.' Once that cleanup is done, the Tier 1 split becomes cleaner: tui_helpers.py gets the 6 genuinely pure functions (_last_modified_key, handle_cli_commands, _handle_config_command, _handle_context_command, _feature_markdown, _escape_markup, _format_json_text — ~225 lines) with explicit named re-exports, and tui_widgets.py gets _build_feature_detail_widgets which now only depends on _escape_markup, _format_json_text, Textual, and Config/load_scripts. For Tier 2, the fourth contributor's resequencing to prioritize BaseModal with shared action_cancel is the right call — but the 8 ModalScreen subclasses also share duplicated compose() boilerplate (title Static + TextArea/Input + Button row pattern) that a BaseModal could template, yielding a larger reduction than just consolidating action_cancel. For _check_for_changes, the real problem revealed by the code (lines 2606-2637) is that _load_features calls FeatureFile.list_all() which does a full directory walk + JSON parse on every invocation, and then line 2636 calls FeatureFile.list_all() again without any board filter for server push — so every 10-second tick parses every JSON file twice. The minimal fix is a module-level LRU cache on FeatureFile.list_all keyed by (board, directory_mtime) that invalidates when the stage directory's mtime changes, avoiding individual file stats entirely."
}
